Package: aprioripowerwizard
Type: project
Title: A Priori Power Analysis Wizard
Version: 1.2.2
Authors@R: person("Federico", "Atzori", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(affiliation = "University of Cagliari"))
Description: A step-by-step Shiny application that guides researchers in
    experimental economics and behavioral science through an a priori
    (before data collection) power analysis to determine required sample
    size, across sixteen closed-form analysis families. Not distributed as
    an installable package; this file documents runtime dependencies and
    metadata for renv and for reviewers, mirroring the version pinned in
    CITATION.cff.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    shiny,
    bslib,
    htmltools,
    pwr,
    ggplot2,
    survival,
    jsonlite
Suggests:
    plotly,
    htmlwidgets,
    rmarkdown,
    tinytex,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    chromote,
    httpuv,
    shinylive
Encoding: UTF-8
URL: https://github.com/federicoatz/apriori-power-wizard, https://federicoatz.com/apriori-power-wizard/
BugReports: https://github.com/federicoatz/apriori-power-wizard/issues
